## ISC's container images

Runtime conventions in these images - config paths, volume layout, exposed
ports and the single-process `CMD` form - deliberately follow ISC's own
`kea-docker` images so that these can serve as drop-in replacements.

No files were copied from `kea-docker`. Its Dockerfiles carry
`SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0` headers; the conventions adopted here are
interface facts about how Kea runs rather than expressive content. This
repository is MPL-2.0 licensed regardless, which matches Kea and removes any
ambiguity.

`kea-docker` upstream: <https://gitlab.isc.org/isc-projects/kea-docker>

## ISC code-signing keys

`build/keys/isc-keyblock.asc` is ISC's published code-signing keyblock,
retrieved from <https://www.isc.org/docs/isc-keyblock.asc>. It is redistributed
unmodified so that tarball signature verification is reproducible and does not
depend on fetching a key at build time.
